            <Folder>
                <UniqueID>a6a39e71a084cd228f4f013</UniqueID>
                <ReadableID/>
                <VersionIdentification>2026/09/09 09:28:25,0 +0000</VersionIdentification>
                <Name>HIL Test</Name>
                <Description>This test group contains the set of test description to be done on HIL system</Description>
                <Reference>Na6a39e71a084cd228f4f014XNa6a39e71a084cd228f4f01300</Reference>
                <DataSource>Test Data</DataSource>
                <Folder>
                    <UniqueID>a6a39e71a084cd228f4f015</UniqueID>
                    <ReadableID>9082946684130130000</ReadableID>
                    <VersionIdentification>2026/09/09 09:28:25,0 +0000</VersionIdentification>
                    <Name>Application CAN Signal Testing</Name>
                    <Description>Feature should get activated on receiving appropriate activation signal and should get deactivated on receiving appropriate deactivation signal or removing activation signal</Description>
                    <Reference>Na6a39e71a084cd228f4f016XNa6a39e71a084cd228f4f01500</Reference>
                    <DataSource>Test Data</DataSource>
                    <TraceItem>
                        <UniqueID>a6a39e71a084cd228f4f017</UniqueID>
                        <ReadableID>9082946684130140000</ReadableID>
                        <VersionIdentification>2026/09/09 09:28:25,0 +0000</VersionIdentification>
                        <Name>TEST.BCM.FUNC.HIL.HLLB.001</Name>
                        <Description>Headlamp LowBeam feature should transmit feature status CAN message when BCM is in ON state.</Description>
                        <Reference>Na6a39e71a084cd228f4f018XNa6a39e71a084cd228f4f01700</Reference>
                        <AdditionalInformation>
                            <Property>
                                <Name>Init Steps</Name>
                                <Value>----------------------------------------
[Description]
Power ON BCM with 24V and 15A supply.
[Actions]
1. Connect BCM to HIL system appropriately
2. Turn ON 24V and 15A supply voltage
[Expected Results]
BCM is getting 24V and 15A supply
----------------------------------------</Value>
                            </Property>
                            <Property>
                                <Name>Run Steps</Name>
                                <Value>----------------------------------------
[Description]
Headlamp LowBeam feature shall transmit feature status CAN message as 0 and 1.
[Actions]
1. Apply high signal (18.5V – 28.5V) on headlamp lowbeam input line (Pin No X).
2. Wait for 3 sec.
3. Check for CAN status message as 1 in headlamp lowbeam CAN status signal (headlamp lowbeam CAN Signal Id).
4. Wait for 3 sec.
5. Apply low signal (0V) on headlamp lowbeam input line (Pin No X).
6. Wait for 3 sec.
7. Check for CAN status message as 0 in headlamp lowbeam CAN status signal (headlamp lowbeam CAN Signal Id).
[Expected Results]
Headlamp LowBeam feature transmits feature status CAN message as 0 when Headlamp LowBeam feature is in OFF state and 1 when Headlamp LowBeam feature is in ON state
----------------------------------------</Value>
                            </Property>
                            <Property>
                                <Name>Shutdown Steps</Name>
                                <Value>----------------------------------------
[Description]
Power OFF BCM i.e., apply 0V and 0A supply.
[Actions]
1. Turn OFF power supply. i.e., apply 0V and 0A supply.
[Expected Results]
BCM is not getting power supply
----------------------------------------</Value>
                            </Property>
                        </AdditionalInformation>
                    </TraceItem>
                    <TraceItem>
                        <UniqueID>a6a39e71a084cd228f4f01f</UniqueID>
                        <ReadableID>9082946684130180000</ReadableID>
                        <VersionIdentification>2026/09/09 09:28:25,0 +0000</VersionIdentification>
                        <Name>TEST.BCM.FUNC.HIL.HLHB.001</Name>
                        <Description>Headlamp HighBeam feature should transmit feature status CAN message when BCM is in ON state.</Description>
                        <Reference>Na6a39e71a084cd228f4f020XNa6a39e71a084cd228f4f01f00</Reference>
                        <AdditionalInformation>
                            <Property>
                                <Name>Init Steps</Name>
                                <Value>----------------------------------------
[Description]
Power ON BCM with 24V and 15A supply.
[Actions]
1. Connect BCM to HIL system appropriately
2. Turn ON 24V and 15A supply voltage
[Expected Results]
BCM is getting 24V and 15A supply
----------------------------------------</Value>
                            </Property>
                            <Property>
                                <Name>Run Steps</Name>
                                <Value>----------------------------------------
[Description]
Headlamp HighBeam feature shall transmit feature status CAN message as 0 and 1.
[Actions]
1. Apply high signal (18.5V – 28.5V) on headlamp highbeam input line (Pin No X).
2. Wait for 3 sec.
3. Check for CAN status message as 1 in headlamp highbeam CAN status signal (headlamp highbeam CAN Signal Id).
4. Wait for 3 sec.
5. Apply low signal (0V) on headlamp highbeam input line (Pin No X).
6. Wait for 3 sec.
7. Check for CAN status message as 0 in headlamp highbeam CAN status signal (headlamp highbeam CAN Signal Id).
[Expected Results]
Headlamp HighBeam feature transmits feature status CAN message as 0 when Headlamp LowBeam feature is in OFF state and 1 when Headlamp HighBeam feature is in ON state
----------------------------------------</Value>
                            </Property>
                            <Property>
                                <Name>Shutdown Steps</Name>
                                <Value>----------------------------------------
[Description]
Power OFF BCM i.e., apply 0V and 0A supply.
[Actions]
1. Turn OFF power supply. i.e., apply 0V and 0A supply.
[Expected Results]
BCM is not getting power supply
----------------------------------------</Value>
                            </Property>
                        </AdditionalInformation>
                    </TraceItem>
                </Folder>
                <Folder>
                    <UniqueID>a6a39e71a084cd228f4f027</UniqueID>
                    <ReadableID>9082946684130220000</ReadableID>
                    <VersionIdentification>2026/09/09 09:28:25,0 +0000</VersionIdentification>
                    <Name>Feature OnOff</Name>
                    <Description>Feature should get activated on receiving appropriate activation signal and should get deactivated on receiving appropriate deactivation signal or removing activation signal</Description>
                    <Reference>Na6a39e71a084cd228f4f028XNa6a39e71a084cd228f4f02700</Reference>
                    <DataSource>Test Data</DataSource>
                    <TraceItem>
                        <UniqueID>a6a39e71a084cd228f4f029</UniqueID>
                        <ReadableID>9082946684130230000</ReadableID>
                        <VersionIdentification>2026/09/09 09:28:25,0 +0000</VersionIdentification>
                        <Name>TEST.BCM.FUNC.HIL.HLLB.002</Name>
                        <Description>Headlamp LowBeam feature should get activated on receiving 24V signal and should get deactivated on receiving 0V signal on input line.</Description>
                        <Reference>Na6a39e71a084cd228f4f02aXNa6a39e71a084cd228f4f02900</Reference>
                        <AdditionalInformation>
                            <Property>
                                <Name>Init Steps</Name>
                                <Value>----------------------------------------
[Description]
Power ON BCM with 24V and 15A supply.
[Actions]
1. Connect BCM to HIL system appropriately
2. Turn ON 24V and 15A supply voltage
[Expected Results]
BCM is getting 24V and 15A supply
----------------------------------------</Value>
                            </Property>
                            <Property>
                                <Name>Run Steps</Name>
                                <Value>----------------------------------------
[Description]
Headlamp lowbeam feature should turn ON and OFF on receiving High (18.5V – 28.5V) and Low (0V) signal respectively on Headlamp lowbeam input line
[Actions]
1. Apply high signal (18.5V – 28.5V) on headlamp lowbeam input line (Pin No X).
2. Wait for 3 sec.
3. Check for output high on headlamp lowbeam output line (Pin No Y).
4. Wait for 3 sec.
5. Apply low signal (0V) on headlamp lowbeam input line (Pin No X).
6. Wait for 3 sec.
7. Check for output low on headlamp lowbeam output line (Pin No Y).
[Expected Results]
Headlamp lowbeam feature gets turned ON on receiving High signal (18.5V – 28.5V) and OFF on receiving Low signal (0V) on Headlamp lowbeam input line
----------------------------------------</Value>
                            </Property>
                            <Property>
                                <Name>Shutdown Steps</Name>
                                <Value>----------------------------------------
[Description]
Power OFF BCM i.e., apply 0V and 0A supply.
[Actions]
1. Turn OFF power supply. i.e., apply 0V and 0A supply.
[Expected Results]
BCM is not getting power supply
----------------------------------------</Value>
                            </Property>
                        </AdditionalInformation>
                    </TraceItem>
